{"title":"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The 1<sup>st</sup> term in a sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the 2<sup>nd</sup> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Each term after that is equal to the sum of the two previous terms in the sequence.\n</p><p>For example, the 3<sup>rd</sup> term in the sequence is equal to the sum of the 1<sup>st</sup> and 2<sup>nd</sup> terms, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97e5b422d9fb083f73e87b6bf3e2bf3dd2161274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 3 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. What is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> term in the sequence?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the sequence is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8dab07337d12ef4294cca8b1b226468ff6b08dd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\text{, }3\\text{, }7\\text{, }10\\text{, }17\\text{, }27\\text{, }44\\text{, }...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 2\">player 2</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d198c9c5956d17907f8136cc45fd6e45dcfa5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Using our sequence we see that the 6<sup>th</sup> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c53cf1ee0e5e31d7791ca7394346930c8a03dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC\">2023 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 2\">Relay C Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.ph